DB::close() drops the error of its final fdatasync, trim or hint write and
returns as if every acknowledged write were durable: the silent shutdown
close() was added to end. Reverts #260's report (#257).
Rare in a full run (a failed writeback and an eviction before a clean
close, about one life in 300), so every life ends in a clean close:
Disable: power,sigkill
Guarded-by: "close() throws when its fdatasync fails, closes all the same, and a reopen recovers what was durable"

diff --git a/bytecaskdb/bytecask.cppm b/bytecaskdb/bytecask.cppm
index aab1a99e..ac0af9a2 100644
--- a/bytecaskdb/bytecask.cppm
+++ b/bytecaskdb/bytecask.cppm
@@ -2783,7 +2783,6 @@ void DB::close() {
     ::close(lock_fd_);
     lock_fd_ = -1;
   }
-  if (error) std::rethrow_exception(error);
 }
 
 #pragma endregion
